    "id": "train-2735",
    "question": "Bob gets paid $5 an hour for the regular hours he works and $6 an hour for any overtime hours he works. All hours over 40 in a week are considered overtime. If Bob works 44  hours in the first week and 48 hours in the second week, how much did he make?",
    "gold": "472",
    "answer": "Bob has worked 40 hours/week x 2 weeks = <<40*2=80>>80 regular hours\nBob got paid 80 hours x $5/hour = $<<80*5=400>>400 for his regular hours\nBob worked 44 hours - 40 hours = <<44-40=4>>4 hours of overtime in the first week\nBob worked 48 hours - 40 hours = <<48-40=8>>8 hours of overtime in the second week\nIn total Bob worker 8 hours + 4 hours =<<8+4=12>>12 hours of overtime.\nBob got paid $6/hour x 12 hours = $<<6*12=72>>72 for overtime\nIn 2 weeks Bob earned $400 + $72 = $<<400+72=472>>472\n#### 472"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Bob made in the two weeks, we need to calculate his earnings for each week separately and then sum them up.\n\n**First Week:**\n- Bob works 44 hours in the first week.\n- Regular hours: 40 hours\n- Overtime hours: 44 - 40 = 4 hours\n\nThe earnings for the first week are calculated as follows:\n- Regular hours earnings: \\(40 \\text{ hours} \\times \\$5/\\text{hour} = \\$200\\)\n- Overtime hours earnings: \\(4 \\text{ hours} \\times \\$6/\\text{hour} = \\$24\\)\n- Total earnings for the first week: \\$200 + \\$24 = \\$224\n\n**Second Week:**\n- Bob works 48 hours in the second week.\n- Regular hours: 40 hours\n- Overtime hours: 48 - 40 = 8 hours\n\nThe earnings for the second week are calculated as follows:\n- Regular hours earnings: \\(40 \\text{ hours} \\times \\$5/\\text{hour} = \\$200\\)\n- Overtime hours earnings: \\(8 \\text{ hours} \\times \\$6/\\text{hour} = \\$48\\)\n- Total earnings for the second week: \\$200 + \\$48 = \\$248\n\n**Total Earnings:**\n- Total earnings for both weeks: \\$224 + \\$248 = \\$472\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{472}\\).",
